Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2: describe the SPI NOR
 supply

The SPI NOR core requests a "vcc" supply for the flash, which is not
described for the Orange Pi Zero2, so it falls back to the dummy
regulator and logs at boot:

  spi-nor spi0.0: supply vcc not found, using dummy regulator

The 2MiB SPI NOR flash hangs off SPI0 on the PC bank and, per the
Orange Pi Zero2 v1.3 schematic, is powered from the 3.3V VCC-IO rail
generated by ALDO1, which already sources VCC-PC here.

The PL bank's "vcc-pl" supply is deliberately left undescribed: PL0/PL1
carry the RSB bus to the AXP305 that generates ALDO1, so naming ALDO1
as the PL supply creates a probe-order cycle (pinctrl waits for the
regulator, the regulator's PMIC waits for the RSB pins) and the PMIC,
and with it MMC and Ethernet, never probes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -153,3 +153,9 @@
 	vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 	vcc-pi-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 };
+
+&spi0 {
+	flash@0 {
+		vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+	};
+};
